<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="descriptionview.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="descriptionview">
    <!-- game::extended_description (examine-tile description view). A clean text
         pane: the host builds one colour-tagged `desc` string per frame from the
         creature / furniture / terrain extended_description() (+ signage), and
         this doc renders it. The whole `desc` is run through cata_text_to_rml in
         one pass (so colour tags match correctly across newlines and \n becomes
         <br/>), bound as `body_rml`. `hint_rml` is the top key-hint bar
         ([c] creatures / [f] furniture / [t] terrain / [close]). Render-only:
         keyboard owns the CREATURE/FURNITURE/TERRAIN/QUIT actions. -->
    <div class="panel desc-panel">
        <div class="desc-head" data-rml="hint_rml"></div>
        <div class="desc-body scroll-pane">
            <div class="desc-text" data-rml="body_rml"></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
